1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,710
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,450
Hello.

5
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:08,650
(Episode 42)

6
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,040
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

7
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,440
You called for me, sir?

8
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:40,610
Yes. When is
the scholarship foundation's...

9
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:41,750
extraordinary board meeting scheduled?

10
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,220
It's scheduled in a week's time.

11
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:47,720
Is there any movement
from my wife's side?

12
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,590
With the goal of passing
the scholarship program,

13
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,020
it seems they're completely
reviewing the proposal.

14
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:56,130
Will that really change the outcome?

15
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:59,830
They should manage the people
before the proposal.

16
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:03,570
You're keeping tabs
on the board members, right?

17
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,340
Yes, I've been checking
on them constantly.

18
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:10,410
Good. Don't miss a single person,
and keep a close eye on them.

19
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:12,010
Yes, sir.

20
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,410
By the way,

21
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:17,750
it looks like you had lunch
with the director...

22
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:19,280
from Cheongma Foods today.

23
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:21,820
Yes, I did.

24
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:26,590
I didn't know you two were
this close until today.

25
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:30,700
Well, we see each other
occasionally, if not often.

26
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,560
He's a decent man, you see.

27
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:37,440
He isn't frivolous,
but serious and steadfast.

28
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:40,710
Right. I see.

29
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,880
Serious and steadfast?

30
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:49,210
Of course he is,
with all the money he's been fed.

31
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,120
He'll at least pretend
to play along.

32
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,350
How simple-minded.

33
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,120
Kang Young Hoon.

34
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,860
The more I dig,
the more interesting it gets.

35
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,330
When should I drop this bomb?

36
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:09,570
Did you hear the news?

37
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:12,170
Ms. Kang and Chief Cha
are getting engaged soon.

38
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:13,270
Really?

39
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:15,270
Are they actually
getting married this time?

40
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:17,810
Should we prepare a small cake
for the meeting?

41
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:21,150
That sounds great.
Ms. Kang will probably love it.

42
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,380
Eun Seol,
you'll pitch in too, right?

43
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,120
Pitch in for what?

44
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:28,250
Ms. Kang and Chief Cha
are getting engaged.

45
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:30,990
We're getting them a cake
at the next meeting.

46
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:35,730
This would be a great chance
to score points with Ms. Kang.

47
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,030
Sure, I'll pitch in.

48
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:43,030
The date for
the extraordinary board meeting is set,

49
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:44,900
but my heart feels so heavy.

50
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:48,970
We need at least one more person
to come over to our side.

51
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:50,910
It seems the neutral members...

52
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:53,550
have shifted their support
to the CEO,

53
00:02:54,010 --> 00:02:55,150
which is worrying.

54
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,120
I know.

55
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:01,320
At this rate, it won't be easy
to win back their votes.

56
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,720
Don't worry too much, ma'am.

57
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:05,990
At this extraordinary board meeting,

58
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:07,930
we'll definitely be able
to settle this.

59
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:09,660
You think we have a chance?

60
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:13,730
Did you find another way
to sway the directors?

61
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,930
Not the directors.

62
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,370
I found a way to change
the CEO's mind.

63
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,410
Persuading the CEO won't be easy.

64
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:27,810
He's someone who prioritizes
the corporate image above all else.

65
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:30,580
And our scholarship program...

66
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,750
doesn't align with the image
the company pursues.

67
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,290
I'll definitely change
the CEO's mind.

68
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:43,960
All right. I'll trust you.

69
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:49,030
Seeing how confident you are,

70
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,300
I trust you even though
I don't fully get what's going on.

71
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,710
If it's too difficult
for you to handle alone,

72
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:55,940
please tell me anytime.

73
00:03:56,510 --> 00:03:57,740
I'll help with anything.

74
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:03,110
(Joo Mi Ran's Background Report)

75
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,180
(Joo Ae Sook, Taeseon Hospital)

76
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,620
(Discharged postpartum)

77
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,680
(Another guardian takes the newborn)

78
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:07,850
(Renamed in October 2000)

79
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:11,290
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

80
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:18,200
Digging deeper into Director Joo
is way too dangerous right now.

81
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,600
If I act rashly,

82
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:23,900
there's no telling
what she might do to Eun Seol.

83
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,210
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

84
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,580
Hello?

85
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:40,220
Hyun Hee, you answered the phone.

86
00:04:41,050 --> 00:04:43,220
You remember me, right?
This is Attorney Seo Hyun Jae.

87
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:47,030
I wanted to help you,
so I contacted you again.

88
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:48,930
Are you really...

89
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,960
going to help me?

90
00:04:54,530 --> 00:04:56,570
Yes, of course.

91
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:01,140
Ko Eun Seol talked that big a game?

92
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,610
It didn't seem like empty words.

93
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,810
It seemed like
she had a special trick...

94
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:09,610
to change the CEO's mind
and win the votes of the directors.

95
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:10,950
I'm sure she does.

96
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:14,890
She isn't the type
to talk big with nothing to show.

97
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:18,820
So keep your eyes on her
every second.

98
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:22,230
Right. I'll do my best.

99
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,430
Why? Is there a problem?

100
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,000
No, ma'am.

101
00:05:28,230 --> 00:05:31,640
I'll stay closer to her
and keep a close watch.

102
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,740
But don't be too obvious about it.

103
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,580
She's just as sharp as you,

104
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,480
so keep a safe distance
while you read her.

105
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,180
Yes, I'll do that.

106
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:51,020
Are you really not going
to tell me anything either?

107
00:05:51,590 --> 00:05:52,590
About what?

108
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:54,060
Your secret plan...

109
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,230
to change the CEO's mind.

110
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,560
Oh, that.

111
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:01,330
I'm keeping it a secret
so I can surprise everyone.

112
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,170
That's why
I didn't even tell the Chairman.

113
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:06,840
But we're on the same team.

114
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:08,770
I'm a little disappointed.

115
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:14,580
Secretary Choi,
are you hiding something from me?

116
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:17,150
Am I hiding something?

117
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:20,050
Of course not.

118
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:23,550
When we first met,
I told you everything about my past.

119
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:25,960
I never talk about my past...

120
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:28,860
to anyone, no matter who they are.

121
00:06:31,330 --> 00:06:34,270
Those times
might've been painful back then,

122
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,500
but put together, they're ultimately
what made you who you are today.

123
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,370
Of course, the same goes for me.

124
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:45,780
People look
at my ten unjust years in prison...

125
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,880
and call my past tragic and pitiful,

126
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:51,180
but I don't necessarily think so.

127
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:52,680
Then,

128
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:56,090
can you speak about it openly
anywhere you go?

129
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:58,820
About your past, I mean.

130
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,190
Of course.

131
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:04,700
If I don't want to lose to my past,

132
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,760
I have to be the first
to acknowledge...

133
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,170
and embrace those times.

134
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:16,610
Our Hae Ra finally got her wish.

135
00:07:17,110 --> 00:07:18,910
It's just an engagement,

136
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,910
but given how much
you were rushing to get married,

137
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:24,350
your dad really compromised for you.

138
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:25,980
I know.

139
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,850
But why did Dad suddenly
change his mind?

140
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:32,490
I mean, for a while,
he wouldn't even look at Seok Jin.

141
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:35,430
Being told to get engaged
out of the blue...

142
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:36,860
caught me off guard.

143
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:38,230
I know.

144
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:42,030
Your dad wouldn't accept Chief Cha
as his future son-in-law.

145
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:46,140
Honestly, I was a bit surprised too.

146
00:07:46,570 --> 00:07:49,710
Perhaps after having a meal
with So Yeon last time,

147
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,740
he had a change of heart.

148
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:53,740
You think so?

149
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,080
Of course.

150
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:58,780
He was very close with Seong Woo.

151
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,890
After what happened to Seong Woo,

152
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:05,060
he must've felt indebted to So Yeon.

153
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:08,760
Anyway, before Dad
changes his mind again,

154
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:11,600
I should pick out
an engagement dress first.

155
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:15,400
People don't wear dresses
to engagement parties these days.

156
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:18,600
They just have a simple meal
and call it a day.

157
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:20,870
Oh, right.

158
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:23,470
Isn't So Yeon's birthday
in a few days?

159
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:25,580
Should I look into it?

160
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:29,410
Don't you know
when So Yeon's birthday is?

161
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:31,450
No, I don't.

162
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:34,150
You should take care
of things like that...

163
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:36,520
before your engagement dress.

164
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,390
Director Joo.

165
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,330
From now on,
please handle everything...

166
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:43,430
related to So Yeon first.

167
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:47,570
Hae Ra and I will likely forget
from time to time.

168
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,570
Yes, I'll do that.

169
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:54,070
Mom, come on.

170
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:58,880
- I'm home.
- Wait. What's this?

171
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,210
This?

172
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:03,480
I won first place
at the sports day today.

173
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:05,350
This was the prize.

174
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:08,250
Why are you doing a sports day
at your age?

175
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:10,590
A neighborhood athletic meet
would make more sense.

176
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,160
Teun Teun's kindergarten had
a family sports day today.

177
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,660
- What...
- What?

178
00:09:14,730 --> 00:09:16,030
A family sports day?

179
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,130
You, come here and sit down.

180
00:09:21,430 --> 00:09:23,100
Hold on, then.

181
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:24,740
You,

182
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:28,370
Teun Teun's Mom, and Teun Teun.
The three of you went together?

183
00:09:29,010 --> 00:09:30,010
Yes.

184
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:31,510
You fool.

185
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:34,110
You might as well
just take out a billboard.

186
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:36,380
You work at that woman's cafe,

187
00:09:36,710 --> 00:09:38,920
and now you go
to her son's sports day?

188
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:41,620
Don't tell me you've moved in
with her already.

189
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,560
What if rumors start spreading
around the neighborhood?

190
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:46,620
How are you going
to get married later?

191
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:48,160
Here we go again.

192
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,030
You're letting
your imagination run wild.

193
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:52,330
I told you that won't happen.

194
00:09:52,330 --> 00:09:54,300
Hey, your grandmother's right.

195
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:58,370
Why did you have to go?
He has that lawyer uncle.

196
00:09:58,370 --> 00:10:00,370
I just went as Teun Teun's uncle.

197
00:10:00,570 --> 00:10:02,440
His real uncle went
on a business trip,

198
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:03,980
so I went instead.

199
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:06,610
Look.

200
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,980
(Uncle)

201
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,380
Then, you punk,

202
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,580
I should've gone with you.

203
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,490
- You?
- Exactly.

204
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:16,050
I may not look it,
but back in the day,

205
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,920
I was a tug-of-war champion.
Don't you remember?

206
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:22,390
Back during your sports days,
the team I was on always won.

207
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:23,490
Hold on.

208
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,630
Can someone even say
they're good at tug-of-war?

209
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:29,530
I mean, you just ride on
everyone else's coattails.

210
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:32,100
Hey, in life,

211
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:35,040
riding on other people's coattails
is the easiest way to go.

212
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:37,170
Riding coattails
is an art form, you know.

213
00:10:37,170 --> 00:10:39,410
Like this.
You grab the rope tightly,

214
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,780
and just lie back.

215
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:43,810
Just stay down and hold tight.

216
00:10:44,850 --> 00:10:47,420
Unbelievable.

217
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,250
As his father,

218
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,420
shouldn't you be worried
that he's spending time...

219
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,320
with a single mother?

220
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:55,230
You've got to be kidding me.

221
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,260
I'd rather die
than suffer like this.

222
00:10:57,330 --> 00:10:59,200
I'd rather die.

223
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:01,770
Mom, what are you so worried about?

224
00:11:01,830 --> 00:11:04,400
Eun Guk knows what he's doing.

225
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:07,410
Go change out of that!

226
00:11:12,910 --> 00:11:16,050
Hey, is there really nothing
between you and Teun Teun's Mom?

227
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:19,180
What could be between us?

228
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:22,950
I'm being very serious right now.

229
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,660
Do you by any chance
like Teun Teun's Mom?

230
00:11:27,730 --> 00:11:29,230
Like her? Oh, please.

231
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,630
No way.

232
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:33,230
I just adore Teun Teun,

233
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,200
and the boss looks out for me.

234
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:37,230
I'm just mostly grateful.

235
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:40,100
If that's really all it is, fine.

236
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:46,440
But if you happen to fall for her,
you'd better tell me.

237
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:50,210
I know I can't do much as a father,

238
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,250
but if you're really sincere,

239
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:53,720
I'll...

240
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:56,320
always stand by you.

241
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,160
Back to bed, then.

242
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:12,570
Thanks to you,
we finally have an oven at home.

243
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,940
You earned it yourself
by coming in first place.

244
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:20,080
But honestly,
how epic was that match?

245
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:23,710
Has a three-legged race
ever been that dramatic?

246
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:28,420
You almost tripped
right at the finish line,

247
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,620
so I scooped you up
and ran with you in my arms.

248
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,520
What do you mean, in your arms?

249
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:34,860
Come on.

250
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:36,560
That definitely counts
as being held.

251
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,600
Boss, you clung to me while I ran.

252
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,800
No way!

253
00:12:41,070 --> 00:12:44,170
You practically dragged me along
instead of carrying me in your arms.

254
00:12:44,570 --> 00:12:47,170
This is all thanks
to my regular workouts...

255
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,840
and these muscles, right?

256
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:52,280
Using all my arm strength,
I grabbed you...

257
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:53,410
Enough.

258
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:56,580
Hurry up with that
and bring the coffee beans.

259
00:12:56,810 --> 00:12:57,920
Rather than that...

260
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:00,250
Here. Feel them. Go ahead.

261
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:05,020
These are the real MVPs
behind our win yesterday.

262
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:08,760
What do you think?
Impressive, right?

263
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:10,290
Impressive, my foot.

264
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,130
Don't be gross!

265
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,870
Boss, why were you clinging
to me yesterday...

266
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,770
if you're this strong?

267
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:20,800
Why do you keep saying
I clung to you?

268
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:24,940
Oh, please. You were totally
snuggling into me yesterday.

269
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:26,480
Just get the coffee beans, will you?

270
00:13:27,810 --> 00:13:30,110
Okay, fine. I'll get them right now.

271
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:36,650
He didn't even finish
mopping the floor.

272
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:39,420
In the early design stage,

273
00:13:39,490 --> 00:13:41,760
instead of forcing the cost ratios,

274
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:44,400
our focus should be on
perfecting the fit.

275
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:46,030
Please polish up those details...

276
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:47,430
so we can review them
at the next meeting.

277
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:48,830
Chief, just a second.

278
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:52,240
A design document's missing,
so I'll go grab it.

279
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,370
Sure, go ahead.

280
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:56,010
Seriously?

281
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:58,080
You should've mentioned it
before the meeting.

282
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,180
We'll review the fabric
and wrap up the meeting.

283
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,250
Sure.

284
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:12,190
<i>Congratulations on your engagement</i>

285
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:15,290
<i>Congratulations on your engagement</i>

286
00:14:15,530 --> 00:14:18,930
<i>Chief Cha and Ms. Kang</i>

287
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,670
<i>Congratulations on your engagement</i>

288
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:25,340
Come on. When did you prepare this?

289
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,570
Hurry and blow out the candles.

290
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,870
- Seok Jin, come on.
- Sure.

291
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:32,940
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations.

292
00:14:33,010 --> 00:14:34,010
Thanks.

293
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,180
I didn't expect you
to do this for us.

294
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:37,950
I'm so touched.

295
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:41,190
- Seok Jin.
- Yes?

296
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:42,490
Aren't you going to say something?

297
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:44,990
Oh, right. Thank you.

298
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:47,490
We sincerely congratulate you two
on your engagement.

299
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:51,200
Thanks. My team is the best.

300
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,100
Ms. Ko.

301
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,470
Eun Seol, could you
take a picture of us?

302
00:14:57,970 --> 00:15:01,140
You got us a cake,
so we should leave a picture.

303
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:03,570
Of course.
You definitely need a picture.

304
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,810
Why? Don't you want to do it?

305
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,480
I do. I'll take it.

306
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:19,620
(Sincere Congratulations
on Your Engagement)

307
00:15:19,690 --> 00:15:22,830
Here we go. 1, 2, 3.

308
00:15:27,730 --> 00:15:29,400
Eun Seol, have some water.

309
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:31,670
- Here.
- Sure.

310
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:40,740
Eun Seol, will you be okay?
The interview is starting soon.

311
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,280
You must be very nervous.

312
00:15:43,710 --> 00:15:46,120
I'm okay. How long until we start?

313
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,450
Hold on.

314
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:49,190
About ten minutes.

315
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,520
Got it.

316
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:52,920
Since it's streaming live online,

317
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:54,330
you'll probably be
even more nervous.

318
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:57,160
Right. I guess I'm a little nervous.

319
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:00,700
You say that now, Eun Seol,

320
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:03,370
but on camera, you'll act
like a total professional.

321
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:07,740
- Will I?
- Of course.

322
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,070
You were like that during
the design competition last time.

323
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:11,610
I knew it then.

324
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:14,680
You're completely made
for the stage, Eun Seol.

325
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:20,020
I'll do great, right?

326
00:16:23,090 --> 00:16:24,890
Rather than trying to do well,

327
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:29,090
just view it as a calm confession
of how you really feel.

328
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,860
Yes, I'll do that.

329
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:37,070
Named as a suspect
in a tragic incident,

330
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:41,170
Ko Eun Seol joins us today
after serving ten years in prison.

331
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,770
Recently, a key suspect...

332
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:46,180
from the original incident
has come forward,

333
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,310
and we understand
you're seeking a retrial.

334
00:16:48,810 --> 00:16:51,520
What kind of story
will you be telling us here today?

335
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:55,090
Hello. I'm Ko Eun Seol,
currently employed at Cheongma...

336
00:16:55,090 --> 00:16:56,450
following my release from prison.

337
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:58,490
Today, I want to talk about...

338
00:16:58,490 --> 00:17:00,190
the Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation's...

339
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:01,530
rehabilitation program.

340
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,400
This program
was actually envisioned...

341
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:05,830
by Chairman Kim Jung Sun...

342
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:07,770
- Eun Seol.
- from the very beginning.

343
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:10,330
Is this what you've been
secretly working on?

344
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:12,540
That's why I'm here today.

345
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,440
The Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation...

346
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:16,640
is pushing this program...

347
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:19,640
to prevent recidivism by helping
former inmates stand on their own,

348
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:23,950
and ultimately, to foster
social stability and integration.

349
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,890
Instead of just providing
one-time financial aid,

350
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:31,490
we aim to support them
past their release,

351
00:17:31,490 --> 00:17:33,820
helping them reintegrate
into society as healthy members...

352
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:36,730
through a long-term support network.

353
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:41,500
Throughout my ten years in prison,
it was the belief...

354
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,400
that the truth...

355
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:46,100
never dies...

356
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,810
that kept me going.

357
00:17:49,410 --> 00:17:50,670
(Current Affairs On: Ko Eun Seol
on the Rehabilitation Scholarship)

358
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:52,580
I won't ever give up.

359
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:54,610
I'm going to prove my innocence...

360
00:17:54,910 --> 00:17:58,350
and uncover the hidden truth
for the whole world to see.

361
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:04,660
And finally,

362
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:07,460
to those who find themselves
in my shoes,

363
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:12,360
I want to tell you
to never lose hope.

364
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,300
Please, keep on living.

365
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:18,200
As long as you keep living,

366
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:22,810
you'll eventually find someone warm
to hold your hand.

367
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:27,740
What on earth was that interview?
Did my wife know about it?

368
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:31,620
I believe Ko Eun Seol planned this
on her own.

369
00:18:34,450 --> 00:18:35,720
How is the public reacting?

370
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:38,820
The public response
is pretty strong.

371
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:42,190
My wife's momentum
won't be easily broken.

372
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:47,000
I might lose my grip
on the foundation entirely.

373
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,670
Since it's come to this,

374
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:51,640
it'd be best for you
to make the first move.

375
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:54,840
What do you mean by that?

376
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:58,780
After you throw your support
behind the program,

377
00:18:59,310 --> 00:19:00,810
we can make it look like...

378
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:04,350
the rest of the board members
are naturally following your lead.

379
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:07,450
That way, even if
the scholarship program passes,

380
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:10,520
all the credit will ultimately
go to you, sir.

381
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,460
Will it really work out like that?

382
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:18,400
I'll tip off the board members
and the Chairman early,

383
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:21,630
letting them know
you're leaning toward supporting it.

384
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:24,600
Right, okay.

385
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:26,970
Go ahead and work on that.

386
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:47,260
Those times
might've been painful back then,

387
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:51,430
but put together, they're ultimately
what made you who you are today.

388
00:19:53,030 --> 00:19:54,700
If I don't want to lose to my past,

389
00:19:55,170 --> 00:19:57,230
I have to be the first
to acknowledge...

390
00:19:57,670 --> 00:19:58,900
and embrace those times.

391
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:08,610
Please, keep on living.

392
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:11,350
As long as you keep living,

393
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:15,850
you'll eventually find someone warm
to hold your hand.

394
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,110
Ko Eun Seol...

395
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:44,780
What exactly are you?

396
00:20:49,890 --> 00:20:53,660
Throughout my ten years in prison,
it was the belief...

397
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:55,630
that the truth...

398
00:20:56,430 --> 00:20:58,230
never dies...

399
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:01,000
that kept me going.

400
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:05,670
Throughout my ten years in prison,
it was the belief...

401
00:21:05,670 --> 00:21:07,570
Hey, it's the nice lady.

402
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:09,770
Mom, I thought you'd be in bed.

403
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,240
I wasn't.

404
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:14,780
By the way,
is that nice lady appearing on TV?

405
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:18,050
I want to watch too.
Let's watch it together.

406
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:19,980
I'm going to prove my innocence...

407
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:21,350
Do you like the nice lady that much?

408
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:26,220
Of course. I was actually
hoping to see her.

409
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:27,690
And finally...

410
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:31,800
I want to eat tteokbokki
with the nice lady again.

411
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,760
Never lose hope.

412
00:21:35,070 --> 00:21:36,070
Mom,

413
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,070
you can't see the nice lady anymore.

414
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,740
Why not?

415
00:21:42,410 --> 00:21:45,380
I want to eat tteokbokki
with the nice lady...

416
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:48,050
and draw with her.

417
00:21:48,050 --> 00:21:49,710
Hae Ra draws well too,

418
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,210
and she likes tteokbokki.

419
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,490
I told you. I really...

420
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:58,490
- hate Hae Ra.
- Mom.

421
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:02,660
I'm getting engaged to her.

422
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:06,460
What's an engagement?

423
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:09,570
We're promising to get married,
and we will eventually.

424
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:14,670
No. Absolutely not.

425
00:22:16,170 --> 00:22:17,170
Mom.

426
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:20,580
If you marry Hae Ra,

427
00:22:21,710 --> 00:22:23,310
my husband will be sad.

428
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:26,050
He'll cry from up above.

429
00:22:26,820 --> 00:22:30,520
You can't marry Hae Ra.
Don't marry her, Mr. Seok Jin.

430
00:22:31,190 --> 00:22:32,320
Mom, why are you being like this?

431
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:35,530
You just can't. Absolutely not.

432
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:36,930
I hate it.

433
00:22:44,970 --> 00:22:48,470
I didn't know you were planning
an interview like that.

434
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:52,710
The public reaction is way bigger
than expected.

435
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:56,380
Honestly, I didn't expect
such a huge reaction either.

436
00:22:57,150 --> 00:22:58,650
More than
the scholarship program itself,

437
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:02,390
it's your personal story
that really hit home for people.

438
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,120
It didn't feel like
some calculated strategy.

439
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:06,960
People really felt...

440
00:23:07,660 --> 00:23:09,160
your sincerity first.

441
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:12,200
Thanks to this,
Cheongma's reputation...

442
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:16,000
through the scholarship program
will soar.

443
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:18,700
Eun Seol, like you said,

444
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:22,140
the CEO has no reason
to oppose it now.

445
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:24,370
Eun Seol.

446
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:27,010
Great work.

447
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,150
Thank you.

448
00:23:31,150 --> 00:23:34,020
So, did you inform the board
of my intentions?

449
00:23:34,450 --> 00:23:35,450
Yes.

450
00:23:35,490 --> 00:23:38,120
I carefully expressed
your intentions.

451
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:39,490
Good.

452
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:42,860
Then the board of directors
will follow my lead.

453
00:23:43,330 --> 00:23:45,160
If the vote is unanimous,

454
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:47,700
everyone will think
it's my achievement.

455
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:50,770
Yes, they will see it that way.

456
00:23:52,870 --> 00:23:56,010
As for the scholarship program,
let's wrap it up here.

457
00:23:56,670 --> 00:24:01,010
Let's see how arrogant she gets
over just one scholarship program.

458
00:24:02,580 --> 00:24:05,650
And I thought
I should tell you in advance.

459
00:24:07,020 --> 00:24:09,290
I'm planning to visit
Chief Cha's mother.

460
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:13,120
You're going to see So Yeon?

461
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:14,790
Yes.

462
00:24:14,790 --> 00:24:17,130
There are preparations to make
for the engagement party,

463
00:24:17,390 --> 00:24:20,100
and I'd like to check on her health.

464
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:23,470
Since the Chairman
is busy with work,

465
00:24:23,730 --> 00:24:25,600
I'll be taking care of that.

466
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:28,570
In that case...

467
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:33,510
Can you also keep me updated
on So Yeon's health...

468
00:24:34,410 --> 00:24:35,850
and her overall situation?

469
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:40,550
- Excuse me?
- You saw it too that day.

470
00:24:41,420 --> 00:24:44,120
So Yeon's sudden outbursts
catch people off guard.

471
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:48,230
Since you're checking on her anyway,

472
00:24:48,630 --> 00:24:51,160
I'd like a report
on her condition as well.

473
00:24:52,830 --> 00:24:54,630
Yes, I understand.

474
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:56,770
Regarding So Yeon,

475
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:59,300
I'll report everything
down to the last detail.

476
00:24:59,770 --> 00:25:01,500
Good, thank you.

477
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,480
Can I help you with that?

478
00:25:10,110 --> 00:25:11,110
What?

479
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:19,660
That's it.

480
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:24,390
You truly can do it all,
Director Joo.

481
00:25:25,030 --> 00:25:28,300
It feels like the knots
are finally loosening up.

482
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,000
You must have a lot
on your mind lately.

483
00:25:32,670 --> 00:25:34,770
I'll relieve your stress like this
from time to time.

484
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:41,280
Thank you, Director Joo.

485
00:25:46,780 --> 00:25:47,820
Come in.

486
00:25:54,020 --> 00:25:56,730
This is the press briefing material
that has passed legal review.

487
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:01,030
Great work.

488
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:06,440
How are the preparations
for Ko Eun Seol's retrial going?

489
00:26:08,310 --> 00:26:09,940
Yes, it's currently in progress.

490
00:26:10,670 --> 00:26:13,010
I saw her interview yesterday,

491
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:17,710
and it seems people
are quite supportive of her retrial.

492
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:22,350
Have you turned up anything
on Manager Na?

493
00:26:22,690 --> 00:26:24,990
Since you brought it up,
let me ask you something.

494
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:28,090
- Anything.
- How did you come to know...

495
00:26:28,090 --> 00:26:29,460
the late Manager Na?

496
00:26:30,060 --> 00:26:32,230
I understand that the two of you
were pretty close.

497
00:26:32,430 --> 00:26:34,630
I hired Manager Na
after his interview.

498
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:37,730
Back in his 20s,
he was exceptionally bright.

499
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:40,040
You didn't know him before that?

500
00:26:40,470 --> 00:26:41,470
That's right.

501
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:43,810
I met him for the first time
at the interview.

502
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,640
If I hadn't hired him back then,

503
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:50,310
that wouldn't have happened
to Eun Seol.

504
00:26:51,510 --> 00:26:54,990
I feel just as indebted to her
as you do, Mr. Seo.

505
00:26:57,790 --> 00:27:00,220
Do you have anything else to ask?

506
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:02,430
Not really.

507
00:27:03,790 --> 00:27:05,830
If you ever have any questions,

508
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:07,430
feel free to ask.

509
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:09,030
I'll answer whatever you need.

510
00:27:10,070 --> 00:27:13,400
Besides, it's way clearer
when you ask me upfront like this.

511
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:15,510
Don't go pulling tricks
behind my back.

512
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:17,370
Just ask me straight out
from now on.

513
00:27:17,410 --> 00:27:19,240
Yes, I'll do that.

514
00:27:27,650 --> 00:27:30,050
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

515
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:35,430
Before Manager Na died,

516
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:37,490
the only people
he stayed in touch with...

517
00:27:37,490 --> 00:27:39,330
were his daughter and Director Joo.

518
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:42,670
Manager Na and Director Joo.

519
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,300
They must have had
a deeper relationship.

520
00:27:48,810 --> 00:27:51,010
What on earth is she hiding?

521
00:27:57,910 --> 00:27:59,120
Hyun Hee, hi.

522
00:27:59,650 --> 00:28:02,290
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

523
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:06,620
I saw your interview yesterday.

524
00:28:07,660 --> 00:28:08,890
You looked really brave.

525
00:28:10,090 --> 00:28:11,760
Thank you for thinking
so highly of me.

526
00:28:12,100 --> 00:28:13,800
It seems the scholarship program
you're pushing for...

527
00:28:13,860 --> 00:28:15,830
will be approved without any issues.

528
00:28:17,170 --> 00:28:18,170
Congratulations in advance.

529
00:28:22,970 --> 00:28:24,840
Congratulations to you too, Chief.

530
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,810
On your engagement to Ms. Kang.

531
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,750
I mean it.

532
00:28:36,820 --> 00:28:39,190
I'm truly happy for you.

533
00:28:42,830 --> 00:28:45,760
So you don't need
to feel uncomfortable around me.

534
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,630
Right, thank you.

535
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:00,540
Eun Seol.

536
00:29:05,980 --> 00:29:07,420
If you're free,

537
00:29:07,920 --> 00:29:09,820
how about we grab some tea?

538
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:17,530
You said you could help me, right?

539
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,200
Yes.

540
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:22,100
There are a few suspicions...

541
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:23,930
regarding Manager Na.

542
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:27,270
I'd like to hear
what you have to say...

543
00:29:28,040 --> 00:29:31,340
and help you out
if there's anything I can do.

544
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:36,580
Helping you is also a way...

545
00:29:37,450 --> 00:29:39,450
to uncover the truth
behind the incident.

546
00:29:43,190 --> 00:29:44,190
Then...

547
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:56,800
My dad told me this.

548
00:29:57,770 --> 00:29:59,770
If something ever happened to him,

549
00:30:00,070 --> 00:30:02,140
I'm supposed to take this
to the police.

550
00:30:03,710 --> 00:30:04,910
It's possible...

551
00:30:05,410 --> 00:30:08,650
my dad knew something
was going to happen to him.

552
00:30:11,610 --> 00:30:13,080
May I take a look?

553
00:30:18,390 --> 00:30:20,920
But the police
didn't think much of it.

554
00:30:22,390 --> 00:30:24,390
They said something like this
couldn't be evidence.

555
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,860
(Joo Ae Sook's Baby (F)
Sept. 11, 2000, 11:05 p.m., 3.28kg)

556
00:30:34,170 --> 00:30:35,270
(With Ae Sook at the orphanage)

557
00:30:35,340 --> 00:30:37,640
With Ae Sook at the orphanage.

558
00:30:42,410 --> 00:30:43,980
I met him for the first time
at the interview.

559
00:30:46,950 --> 00:30:50,520
I was deeply touched
by your interview yesterday, Eun Seol.

560
00:31:17,680 --> 00:31:21,320
(A Trap Called Desire)

561
00:31:21,320 --> 00:31:24,650
Why do those two
keep hanging around each other?

562
00:31:24,650 --> 00:31:26,720
If we keep talking,

563
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:29,630
I might be able to find out
what brought on the shock...

564
00:31:29,730 --> 00:31:31,190
on the day of the accident.

565
00:31:31,190 --> 00:31:33,930
So Yeon's against your engagement?

566
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:36,400
She's throwing a tantrum
like a total child.

567
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,700
It's always Ko Eun Seol with you!

568
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:39,070
Stop comparing me to her.

569
00:31:39,140 --> 00:31:41,240
Why do you keep asking for her
when I'm treating you so well?

570
00:31:41,300 --> 00:31:43,970
Why do you keep eyeing Eun Guk?

571
00:31:43,970 --> 00:31:46,480
What if weird rumors start spreading
before he even gets married?

572
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:49,080
Why are you so wary of Director Joo?

573
00:31:49,150 --> 00:31:51,380
I should warn Director Joo
in advance.

574
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:54,650
I have no clue
why he's suddenly acting like this.

575
00:31:55,150 --> 00:31:57,120
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
